  "articleBody": "After a storm in Abbott, you might notice some dings or marks on your roof and immediately think 'hail damage!' But not every mark is a sign of hail, and differentiating between actual hail impact and other issues is super important for an accurate assessment. It's easy to confuse normal wear and tear or other types of damage with hail, and that's where a detailed hail impact assessment comes in.\n\nHail damage typically leaves specific signs. We're talking about bruising, fractures, or punctures on shingles, or dents on soft metals like vents and gutters. These impacts often have a random pattern but might be concentrated on one side of the roof, depending on the storm's direction. However, what sometimes looks like hail damage could actually be manufacturing defects, normal granule loss from aging, foot traffic, or even wind damage that looks similar but isn't from hail. For instance, a missing shingle might be from wind lifting it, not a hailstone striking it. Without a trained eye, these distinctions are tough to make. A professional assessment confirms if hail actually occurred at your property, what size it was, and the direction it came from, often by checking weather reports and site evidence. They'll inspect impact-prone components beyond just shingles, like siding and windows, and will give you a photo-supported scope of work. This clarity helps ensure you get the right repairs for the actual damage, not just cosmetic conditions.\n\n### How to Compare Your Options\nWhen comparing assessments, look for a written methodology, material-specific knowledge, clear photo labeling, and a report that distinguishes facts from repair recommendations. A qualified expert like Discounted Roofing Co. provides this clarity. Contact us for an honest assessment.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}